{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 120,
    "dDurationMs": 480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's official 2025 was the year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2760,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Creativity seemingly died."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17040,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The bestselling movies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18360,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Zootopia to Jurassic World and\nMission Impossible eight were all sequels,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24000,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or they were remasters like Lilo\nand Stitch and How to Train Your Dragon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28440,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, the best selling video games\nbattlefield six, Borderlands"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32320,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "four, Madden 26 were all big franchises\nor remasters like Oblivion Remastered."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38400,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, names\nthat we've seen for decades like Lady"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41000,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gaga, Billie Eilish and Bruno Mars\nonce again dominated the music charts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45320,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now 2025 was not an exceptional year\nin that regard."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49520,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Take a look at this chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50880,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "30 years ago,\nonly about one quarter of the top 20"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54000,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "movies were sequels,\nspinoffs, prequels, or remakes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57240,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now it's close to 90%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59440,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly,\nalmost all of the top selling video games"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now come from established franchises."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65400,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even books show this very same trend."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67920,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The share of top selling titles\nwritten by an already famous"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71640,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "author is increasing each year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75000,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But wasn't\nthe internet supposed to do the opposite?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82880,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the early 2000s, wired"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84760,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "editor in chief Chris Anderson\nfamously predicted that as the internet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 89080,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "made it cheaper and cheaper\nto send songs, movies and games"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92800,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to customers around the world,\nthis would enable niche creators to rise,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97480,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while it would cause big studios\nto become less powerful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101400,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This theory, the theory of the long\ntail, was a beautiful idea"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106080,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the democratization of culture."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108680,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what went wrong?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110520,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As always on Monday macro\nfor this video, we, a team of economists,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115080,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "went deep into the economic literature\nand summarized all the key insights"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119440,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that can explain why big budget sequels\nare bigger than ever today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124360,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we ask a question\nif the rise of sequels reduced creativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128920,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or if there's actually\na thriving long tail of amazing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132800,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "niche content that you just don't know\nabout hiding below the surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137360,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to answer these questions,\nwe first need to understand how the media"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142640,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "industry used to work the gatekeeper\neconomics of the pre-Internet media."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148800,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's go back to the 1980s."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150760,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now imagine you were a singer and wanted\nto earn a living with your passion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155920,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The odds would be stacked against you\nfrom the very beginning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159280,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, you needed a studio\nfilled with super expensive equipment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162760,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to record your song."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164080,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second, to distribute your song,\nyou needed a factory to press records."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168880,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Third, these records then needed to be\ndistributed to thousands of record shops."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173800,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These record shops had limited\nshelf space, so to convince shops to sell"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177880,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your record, you needed to have\nan existing relationship"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181080,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or prove you were already popular\nby getting airtime on the radio,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184960,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for which again,\nyou also needed the right connections."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188240,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Be short before asking consumers\nif they like their content."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192600,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Aspiring creators\nfirst had to convince gatekeepers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196040,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like record labels to give them a shot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198720,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If granted funding, they could record\nand distribute their music."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203280,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This system did produce many, many songs,\nmovies, and games that actually sold"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208080,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "really well and were loved\nby both consumers and critics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212000,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, as you can imagine,\nthis extra layer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214520,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "killed a lot of films, games, and music\nthat we would have loved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218040,
    "dDurationMs": 600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218640,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some of our most beloved cultural icons\nalmost got stuck with the gatekeepers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223280,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, J.K."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224160,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rowling's Harry Potter book\nwas first rejected by 12 publishers before"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228880,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it was published by Bloomsbury,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230440,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and even the Beatles were rejected\nby nearly every major label"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234480,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in Europe before producer\nGeorge Martin finally signed them in 1962."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238800,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, of course,\nwhen one the cost of recording equipment"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241800,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fell lower and lower, and two the internet\nmade distribution costs almost zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246720,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anderson's long term prediction\nabout the rise of niche media"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250320,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the fall of big, safe\nblockbusters made total sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254480,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yet here we are today\nwith more blockbusters than ever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258200,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So again, what happened\nto the fall of the gatekeepers?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262720,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The digital revolution would revolutionize\nthe media industry into main ways."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268120,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, the internet made distribution\nalmost free."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270880,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Overnight music and movies\nno longer had to be pressed onto CDs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275000,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or DVDs, or sold in physical stores\nwith a few clicks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278760,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "songs and films could be downloaded\nstraight into an iPod or a laptop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282360,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But at first, gatekeepers\ntrying to hold back change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286640,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, after piracy, platforms\nlike Napster, The Pirate Bay and others"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290480,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "devastated the revenue in all creative\nand especially the music industry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294840,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Record labels, publishers and others\nincreasingly brought their content"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298760,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to legal online distribution platforms\nlike Spotify, Netflix and Steam."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304160,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second, digital technologies dramatically\nreduced the cost of creating art."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308760,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Suddenly, you could shoot a movie\non your iPhone or record music"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312000,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a home studio using inexpensive\nmicrophones and software."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315840,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This allowed many artists\nto self-fund their work and distribute it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "online to millions of people, effectively\nbypassing traditional gatekeepers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325080,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So yes, in the early days of the internet,\nthe long tail looked to be coming true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329880,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As you can see here in these graphs\nby economic professor Joel Wold Fogel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335400,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the number of new songs added each year\nrose from about 50,000 in 1988"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340240,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to nearly 350,000 by 2007."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344000,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, the number of US made\noriginal films also exploded,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347400,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "along with self-published book titles\nand television shows."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351440,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the first part of Anderson's prediction\nactually seems to have been through"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355480,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "far lower production costs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356760,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and cheap distribution\nhave led to an explosion in creativity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360560,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The long tail is there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362160,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but while the number of songs, movies\nand shows exploded,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people increasingly spend their money\non consuming sequels and franchises."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369320,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rather than these products."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371520,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373000,
    "dDurationMs": 320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373320,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Research professor Walt Fogel\nfirst looked at two obvious explanations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378600,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first is that while it could be true\nthat many more creative products are made,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382560,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the quality of these\ncould actually be very low."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386440,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To test this hypothesis, Walt\nFogel looked at reviews are independent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390640,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Production is bad,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391720,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "therefore scoring lower review scores\nthan big budget sequels or remakes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395880,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For music,\nthis does not appear to be the case."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398800,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Combining lists of best albums\ninto a critic based quality index."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402440,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He finds that while critics really,\nreally loved music"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405440,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the 1970s, average appreciation\nfor newer music"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409040,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "remained stable after Napster\nrevolutionized song distribution."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413800,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, TV shows\nseemingly only got better."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416640,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This graph shows IMDb ratings for the top\n25 release TV shows, and as more TV"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422240,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shows were made, the average quality\ndid not seem to suffer at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 426560,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finally, for video games,\nwe can also see that as the years pass,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430560,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "independently developed games\nactually increasingly dominate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434480,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "top game lists by critics and audiences\nalike."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438440,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even during the 2025 game awards,\nit was not bestsellers like battlefield"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 442560,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "six, Borderlands four, or Madden 26\nthat dominated the awards,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447000,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but rather smaller, self-published games\nlike Silksong"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450320,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hades\ntwo and Claire Obscure expedition 33."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454080,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So big budget\nfranchises and remakes don't sell more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457680,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they are objectively better\nthan independent productions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461400,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This brings us to about Vogel's\nsecond hypothesis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464320,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that independent productions\nare simply not finding their audience."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468120,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps they lack the marketing budget,\nor perhaps"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470880,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "buyers are just increasingly\nnostalgic and risk averse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475360,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, surprisingly, that does not appear\nto be the case."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478760,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Independent productions\nare actually selling more and more"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481880,
    "dDurationMs": 880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the music industry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482760,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Independent labels were increasingly\npenetrating the Billboard's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486200,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Top 200 during the early internet years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489880,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Also, self-published books\nsuch as, most famously, 50 Shades of Gray"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 494880,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are in fact increasingly amongst\nthe world's best selling books."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498480,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Similarly, in film, independent movies\naccounted for about one quarter of box"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503240,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "office revenues in the 1990s,\nbut by 2012 their share had risen to 40%."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509640,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Independent films also represented\nmore than half of DVD sales."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513160,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then finally on gaming platforms\nthat are easiest to publish for,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517040,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like steam on the PC,\nindependently developed games did account"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521280,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "almost for half the revenue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524640,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 2020\nfor similar to big budget productions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528280,
    "dDurationMs": 1160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why in his book"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529440,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what Fogel does actually argue\nthat the long term prediction was correct."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533400,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The digital revolution did in fact produce\na golden age in media."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538120,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the puzzle is still here, isn't it?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540480,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If creativity has actually flourished,\nthen why do sequels,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544280,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "prequels, and franchises\nseem more dominant than ever?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548200,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Why do blockbuster movies and Triple-A\nvideo"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550960,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "games look increasingly repetitive?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554120,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To understand how both of these trends\ncan be true at the same time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558560,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we need to understand\na different mechanism that has transformed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562280,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the media, which is globalization\nand the economics of the superstar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568640,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Culture markets are what economists call\nsuperstar markets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 573360,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is,\nevery consumer has access to the best"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576560,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "game,\nthe best musician, and the best movie."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580280,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Economists have observed\nthat in these types of markets,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583560,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the very best artists\ntend to become superstars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588000,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To illustrate this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588800,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "principle, economist doctor\nFelix Koenig studied how the staggered"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592680,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rollout of television across the US\ntransformed the fortunes of entertainers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that used to play in bars or local venues\nlike dancers, musicians and comedians."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603120,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 1940s, the distribution of earnings\nfor these entertainers looked like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 608840,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some artists were poorer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610320,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some were rich."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611520,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most earn a decent, normal wage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614080,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After television became widespread,\nthough in the 1970s, entertainers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618480,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who once reached only small audiences\nin clubs could now reach the entire"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623040,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "country, performing directly into people's\nliving rooms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627480,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This transformed\nhow audiences chose what to watch,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631200,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with only a few channels to scan."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632920,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Viewers, of course, switched from\na very funny comedian to the funniest one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637920,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a result, the funniest comedians\ncaptured a disproportionate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641760,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "share of attention and became superstars,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645040,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while merely funny comedians lost\nmost of their audience to the superstars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650160,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not surprisingly, by the 1970s,\nfewer comedians earned ordinary wages,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654600,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while a small fraction\nbecame extraordinarily rich."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658240,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the power of superstar markets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661400,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this brings us back to the graphs\nfrom the introduction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665880,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Movies, video games and books."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668040,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Inside the top 20."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669480,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They all became more concentrated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672360,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This trend happened"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673320,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as digitalization happened\nand the internet became more popular."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677240,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it also happened\nwhen another trend took place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680400,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The globalization of mass media,\nespecially as the English language spread"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 685560,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "across the globe and Asia, got a lot\nricher, creating many more consumers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691080,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Indeed, as you can see here,\nfor most of the 20th century,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694560,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hollywood earned the majority of its box\noffice revenue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697720,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "domestically, with international markets\nplaying a secondary role."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702320,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That pattern has now reversed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704320,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today, most of the theatrical revenue\nfrom major films"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "comes from outside the US and Canada."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710400,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Driven by the expansion of markets\nsuch as China and the growth of English"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714280,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "speaking audiences across\nAsia, Latin America and Europe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718840,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is where superstar economics\nfully comes into play."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723000,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Films\nthat travel best across global markets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726280,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tend to share certain characteristics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728760,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Visual spectacle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 735880,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Familiar franchises."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739880,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And instantly recognizable stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 745200,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you put on some muscle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746800,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you know in this superstar\nenvironment, small differences"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751160,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in quality or recognition\ncan have outside effects."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755080,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Securing a top tier actor, a celebrated\ndirector, a cutting edge CGI crew."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760360,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This can significantly boost\na global box office performance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 764600,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, this brings us\nto the final piece of the puzzle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768080,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is all very expensive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770120,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So as making top tier content became"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772920,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more expensive due to superstar economics,\nit also makes sense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777240,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that investors increasingly demanded safe\nproducts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781120,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This can explain why, in the top\nof the global market, we increasingly saw"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786160,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the production of spectacle,\nhigh budget sequels, spinoffs and remakes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790720,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So globalization can explain why"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792280,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we see more and more concentration\nat the very top."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796080,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to play the blockbuster game,\nyou need to invest more and more."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799160,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the safest way to do\nthat is to focus on sequels and remakes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803320,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But meanwhile, digitization\nand falling production costs"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807040,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can explain why we do actually also see\nan explosion of creativity, creativity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812720,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that is actually both reaching audiences\nand leading to critical acclaim."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817320,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Indeed, as you can see here, for movies,\nwe have seen more and more money available"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821480,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for cheap movies and for blockbusters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824400,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but not for a high value productions\nthat cannot quite be blockbusters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 830680,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Therefore, I'm happy to say"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 831760,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that for this video\nwe have a quite optimistic conclusion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 836040,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, 2025 is not a bad year for pop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838920,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "culture in general, just for the top 20."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 841920,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If, like me, you are fed up with sequels\nand remakes, then actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845640,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is a massive long tail out there\nfor every media category."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849880,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850720,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I really enjoy video games and honestly,\nI'm having more fun than ever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854920,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While I used to play blockbusters\nlike Call of Duty one and Call of Duty two"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858480,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when I was younger last year, I really had\njust as much fun playing independent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 863160,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "games on my Steam Deck, like hotline\nMiami, Bilateral Potato, and Undertale."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869080,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand, for movies,\nI would not know where to look."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872680,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Luckily, through making this video,\nI found out that my colleague"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 875600,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Alejandro is a real independent movie fan"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 878840,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he did not watch blockbusters\nor remakes at all last year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882840,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just amazing titles\nlike the Norwegian Sentimental Value,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 886560,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Spanish Sirat and the Iranian film."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 890120,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was just an accident."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891800,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the real question, in my opinion,\nis actually how do you find the long tail?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896880,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, one of the simplest ways to do\nthis is luckily right here on YouTube."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900960,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just use the search bar\nand type top ten Best independent Games,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 904480,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "best independent Movies, books\nor songs of 2025 or of all time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908760,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there you'll find\nthat creativity has not disappeared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911920,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has split in two with a vast, vibrant,\nlong tail of experimentation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916760,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "coexisting alongside a small number\nof highly optimized blockbusters"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 921240,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that dominate\nour shared cultural spotlight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924080,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But yeah, that's my take.\nWhat do you think?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 926840,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you're interested in in-depth\nfollow up analysis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930240,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about the future of the media industry,\nI highly recommend"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 933280,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you check out our advertising sponsor,\nThe Economist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937200,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Specifically, I recommend you check out\nthis detailed analysis about how Netflix"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 942360,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Paramount's battle for Warner Brothers\nwill determine the future of Hollywood."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947040,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then follow up with this analysis\nabout how actually the real threat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950840,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to big streamers like Netflix comes from\nindependent creators like me on YouTube."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955920,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And finally,\nthis super interesting analysis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 957880,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about how a wave of media\ninnovation is coming from China right now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963080,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The economist delivers insights\nthat help you see the bigger picture."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 967000,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is why I highly recommend\nyou subscribe to The Economist,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970680,
